        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, there is now way of implementing this. The completion list comes from built-in completion mechanism (\"insert completion popup menu\", see `:h ins-completion-menu`) which does not have the way to set borders.\r\n\r\nClosing as (currently) impossible to resolve. If Neovim adds support for that, this should be revisited.",
